# Build-context excludes for runtime/Dockerfile.
#
# WHY THIS FILE AND NOT A REPO-ROOT .dockerignore: the build context is the PARENT of this
# repository (docker-compose.yml sets `context: ..`, and CI checks the repo out into a
# `sellerclaw-agent/` subdirectory and builds with `context: .`), and Docker only ever reads a
# .dockerignore from the context root. A .dockerignore inside this repo is therefore never
# consulted — BuildKit does read `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile, which is
# what this is.
#
# Keep local builds identical to CI. plugins/*/node_modules is gitignored, so a fresh CI clone
# has none, while a contributor who ran `npm install` (or `npm test`) in a plugin used to ship
# ~49 MB of dev-only dependencies — typescript and vitest, nothing the runtime loads — into the
# image, and every reinstall changed the COPY layer and re-ran every step after it.
**/node_modules

# Python build/test droppings from a host-side `uv run pytest`; never referenced by any COPY.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.venv
